{
  "question": "Do the day‑10 resonator_obs measurements represent a genuine upward drift of the instrument (or an environmental effect), or are they consistent with random variation and normal measurement noise?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Instrumental drift in resonator_obs (e.g., temperature‑induced or calibration shift)",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "The six consecutive day‑10 readings (ids 285163, 535732, 67166, 950842, 676763, 873709) average 4.0839, ≈0.027 above the baseline mean (4.0565). Such a systematic offset across multiple trials suggests a possible drift. No comparable upward shift was observed on day 9 (id 499184), so the drift would have begun very recently, consistent with an abrupt environmental change.",
      "evidenceFor": [285163, 535732, 67166, 950842, 676763, 873709],
      "evidenceAgainst": [499184]
    },
    {
      "label": "Random statistical fluctuation within expected instrumental noise",
      "probability": 0.60,
      "rationale": "All instruments display a spread of ≈0.001–0.004 in individual trials; the observed day‑10 spread (≈0.08) is well within the range of past variability. The baseline of 86 readings shows 86 distinct values with a minimum spacing of 0.0001, indicating high resolution and no evidence of systematic bias. The day‑9 reading (id 499184) aligns with the baseline, supporting the view that the day‑10 cluster is a chance aggregation.",
      "evidenceFor": [],
      "evidenceAgainst": [285163, 535732, 67166, 950842, 676763, 873709, 499184]
    },
    {
      "label": "Transient measurement error affecting the day‑10 batch (e.g., operator handling or temporary mis‑calibration)",
      "probability": 0.08,
      "rationale": "A single operator conducted all day‑10 resonator_obs trials; a consistent slip or temporary mis‑setting could produce a uniform offset. No independent verification exists for these specific trials, making an operator‑specific error plausible but less likely than random variation.",
      "evidenceFor": [285163, 535732, 67166, 950842, 676763, 873709],
      "evidenceAgainst": [499184]
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.02,
  "summaryOfChange": "Previous review contained no active hypotheses. I identified the most salient anomaly: a cluster of higher resonator_obs values on day 10. I formulated a new question about whether this indicates drift or random fluctuation. Three hypotheses were introduced (drift, random noise, transient error) with probabilities summed to 1, and a small residual left for unknown factors. Evidence citations were added accordingly."
}

